Context
- User observed an apparent hard limit on how many tool calls can occur in a single message when using function-based tool calling.

Finding
- The cap comes from an AI SDK stop condition (max step count), not a dedicated 'max tool calls' limit.
- Cherry Studio set stopWhen: stepCountIs(20) in src/renderer/src/aiCore/prepareParams/parameterBuilder.ts, which caps the agentic loop to 20 steps per streamText call.

Decision
- Make the step cap configurable via assistant.settings.customParameters.
- Default to unlimited (Infinity) unless the user explicitly sets a value.
- Support both maxSteps and max_steps (and stopWhenMaxSteps) keys.

Implementation
- Added parseMaxSteps() and resolveMaxSteps() in src/renderer/src/aiCore/prepareParams/parameterBuilder.ts.
- stopWhen now uses stepCountIs(resolveMaxSteps(assistant)).
